# C-type dipole yoke - quarter model, HEX mesh
# Canonical geometry: ELF CEFC 2020 C-Type model (yoke.jou -> yoke.step)
# Units: meters
#
# Coordinate system:
#   y = gap direction (pole tip at y~0, main leg at y~0.15)
#   z = beam direction (symmetry at z=0)
#   x = depth/thickness (symmetry at x=0)
#
# Symmetry planes: x=0 and z=0
# Use "Quarter (X,Z)" in Add Kelvin dialog
#
# 3 volumes (NOT united) for structured hex meshing:
#   Vol 1: Pole piece   (near gap)
#   Vol 2: Yoke back    (horizontal return)
#   Vol 3: Main leg     (coil location)
#
# After imprint/merge, shared surfaces ensure continuous mesh.
reset

# === Pole piece (near gap) ===
# ELF: 40mm(y) x 100mm(z) x 25mm(x)
# Quarter: x=[0, 0.0125], y=[0, 0.040], z=[0, 0.050]
brick x 0.0125 y 0.040 z 0.050
move volume 1 x 0.00625 y 0.020 z 0.025

# === Yoke back (horizontal return) ===
# ELF: 80mm(y) x 50mm(z) x 25mm(x)
# Quarter: x=[0, 0.0125], y=[0.040, 0.120], z=[0, 0.025]
brick x 0.0125 y 0.080 z 0.025
move volume 2 x 0.00625 y 0.080 z 0.0125

# === Main leg (where coil sits) ===
# ELF: 62.5mm(y) x 105mm(z) x 25mm(x)
# Quarter: x=[0, 0.0125], y=[0.120, 0.1825], z=[0, 0.0525]
brick x 0.0125 y 0.0625 z 0.0525
move volume 3 x 0.00625 y 0.15125 z 0.02625

# === Imprint/merge for shared surfaces (continuous mesh) ===
imprint volume all
merge volume all

# === Hex mesh ===
volume all scheme map
volume 1 size 0.005
volume 2 size 0.008
volume 3 size 0.006
mesh volume all

# === Blocks ===
set duplicate block elements on
block 1 add volume 1 2 3
block 1 name "yoke"

# === Optional: Air domain for FEM (tet mesh) ===
# Uncomment below for Omega-reduced / A-formulation.
# Not needed for MMM/MSC (Radia integral, natural open BC).
#
# brick x 0.060 y 0.400 z 0.140
# move volume 4 x 0.015 y 0.090 z 0.035
# subtract volume 1 2 3 from volume 4 keep
# imprint volume all
# merge volume all
# volume 4 scheme tetmesh
# volume 4 size 0.015
# mesh volume 4
# block 2 add volume 4
# block 2 name "air"

# Kelvin (FEM only): use 'Add Kelvin' button with 'Quarter (X,Z)' symmetry
